<http://data.silknow.org/object/c5cdd8bb-88c9-357d-b5f7-215215f79793/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Known as 'Sindhi topi' or 'serai topi', these unusual hats were usually made in brightly coloured velvets or flamboyant brocades, as here, always with the contrasting panels at centre back and front of the drum.  They were worn throughout the 19th century by Muslims in Sind.  Originally monopolised by government officials and lawyers, the style also filtered down to other classes of society."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/c5cdd8bb-88c9-357d-b5f7-215215f79793> .

